  "evidencia": "Page: International Imitation Hemingway Competition. Sentence: Also known as \"The Bad Hemingway Contest,\" The International Imitation Hemingway Competition is an annual writing competition begun in Century City, California.\nPage: International Imitation Hemingway Competition. Sentence: Started in 1977 as a \"promotional gag\", and held for nearly thirty years, the contest pays mock homage to Ernest Hemingway by encouraging authors to submit a 'really good page of really bad Hemingway' in a Hemingway-esque style.\nPage: Ernest Hemingway. Sentence: Ernest Miller Hemingway (July 21, 1899 – July 2, 1961) was an American novelist, short story writer, and journalist.\nPage: Ernest Hemingway. Sentence: Hemingway produced most of his work between the mid-1920s and the mid-1950s, and won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1954.",
