        "original_id": "01843bcb-9835-51a9-92a8-4fa2068f9d9b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: International Imitation Hemingway Competition, The Bad Hemingway Contest\n- People: Ernest Hemingway\n- Places: Century City, California\n- Topics: writing competitions, parody, Hemingway-esque style, literature\n\nFacts:\n- Ernest Hemingway was an American novelist, short story writer, and journalist who lived from July 21, 1899 to July 2, 1961.\n- Ernest Hemingway produced most of his work between the mid-1920s and the mid-1950s.\n- Ernest Hemingway won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1954.\n- The International Imitation Hemingway Competition began in 1977 in Century City, California.\n- The International Imitation Hemingway Competition is also known as The Bad Hemingway Contest.\n- The International Imitation Hemingway Competition started as a promotional gag and was held for nearly thirty years.\n- The International Imitation Hemingway Competition pays mock homage to Ernest Hemingway.\n- The International Imitation Hemingway Competition encourages authors to submit a really good page of really bad Hemingway in a Hemingway-esque style.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f463c7ec-9897-521a-bc19-3bff7aaa2332",
